{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Our fathers</b> — This evil that has come upon us is on account of our iniquities, which have joined with the iniquities of our fathers; and they escaped, but we did not. As in the sense of \"visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children\" (Exodus 20:5 [ויקרא כ\"ו] [n: Ibn Ezra cites the concept from Exodus 20:5; the Hebrew does not include a verse reference here, only the phrase פוקד עון אבות על בנים])."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:13.089643315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}